###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# Evaluation times of the models (CPU and GPU) are compared in figures; the
# final models were chosen to evaluate in roughly 100 ms or less.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Only the 'All' rows of Table I are encoded. The per-facet energy errors (H2 on Cu(111), (100), (110), (211)), the per-facet and hydrogen-only force errors, and the standard deviations over the five models are left out.
# - Energy errors are printed in meV (per structure). For MACE the 'correlation order of 2' is encoded as mlips:bodyOrder 2 and 'hidden_irreps 16x0e' as numFeatures 16; for ACE 'correlation order of 4' as bodyOrder 4; for REANN the three message-passing loops as numLayers 3.
# - PaiNN and REANN are new registry methods first used here. Sticking probabilities from MD, minimum-energy paths from climbing-image NEB and phonon band structures have no MetricProperty.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
